WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.292
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online B one, Book three.

2
00:00:05.592 --> 00:00:09.025
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.325 --> 00:00:15.286
Unit one: Personal Identity. Today you will talk about who you are using reflexive pronouns.

4
00:00:15.586 --> 00:00:18.204
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.167 --> 00:00:22.527
Part one: words. You will learn twelve new words.

6
00:00:23.383 --> 00:00:24.605
Identity.

7
00:00:25.617 --> 00:00:28.220
Identity means who you are and what makes you different.

8
00:00:28.817 --> 00:00:30.956
My language is part of my identity.

9
00:00:31.550 --> 00:00:33.959
Your turn. Say: Identity.

10
00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:37.906
Identity.

11
00:00:38.650 --> 00:00:40.104
Individuality.

12
00:00:41.117 --> 00:00:45.252
Individuality means the qualities that make a person different from others.

13
00:00:45.850 --> 00:00:49.243
Our school respects each student's individuality.

14
00:00:49.850 --> 00:00:53.187
Your turn. Say: Individuality.

15
00:00:56.033 --> 00:00:57.371
Individuality.

16
00:00:58.117 --> 00:00:59.338
Self-expression.

17
00:01:00.350 --> 00:01:03.650
Self-expression means showing your feelings and ideas.

18
00:01:04.250 --> 00:01:06.876
Dance is my favourite form of self-expression.

19
00:01:07.483 --> 00:01:10.774
Your turn. Say: Self-expression.

20
00:01:13.633 --> 00:01:15.018
Self-expression.

21
00:01:15.783 --> 00:01:16.703
Values.

22
00:01:17.717 --> 00:01:20.703
Values means your beliefs about what is right and important.

23
00:01:21.317 --> 00:01:23.502
Honesty is one of my core values.

24
00:01:24.117 --> 00:01:26.595
Your turn. Say: Values.

25
00:01:29.433 --> 00:01:30.469
Values.

26
00:01:31.217 --> 00:01:32.020
Belief.

27
00:01:33.017 --> 00:01:35.585
Belief means an idea that you think is true.

28
00:01:36.183 --> 00:01:38.392
I have a strong belief in hard work.

29
00:01:38.983 --> 00:01:41.380
Your turn. Say: Belief.

30
00:01:44.233 --> 00:01:45.211
Belief.

31
00:01:45.950 --> 00:01:47.532
Personality trait.

32
00:01:48.517 --> 00:01:51.747
Personality trait means a quality in your character.

33
00:01:52.350 --> 00:01:55.035
Patience is my best personality trait.

34
00:01:55.650 --> 00:01:58.871
Your turn. Say: Personality trait.

35
00:02:01.733 --> 00:02:03.419
Personality trait.

36
00:02:04.183 --> 00:02:05.289
Authentic.

37
00:02:06.283 --> 00:02:08.782
Authentic means real and true to yourself.

38
00:02:09.383 --> 00:02:12.047
Be authentic. Don't copy other people.

39
00:02:12.650 --> 00:02:14.815
Your turn. Say: Authentic.

40
00:02:17.667 --> 00:02:18.610
Authentic.

41
00:02:19.350 --> 00:02:20.200
Unique.

42
00:02:21.217 --> 00:02:23.483
Unique means the only one of its kind.

43
00:02:24.083 --> 00:02:25.758
Every person is unique.

44
00:02:26.350 --> 00:02:28.654
Your turn. Say: Unique.

45
00:02:31.500 --> 00:02:32.292
Unique.

46
00:02:33.050 --> 00:02:34.063
Confidence.

47
00:02:35.050 --> 00:02:37.433
Confidence means believing in yourself.

48
00:02:38.017 --> 00:02:40.225
Speaking in class gave me confidence.

49
00:02:40.817 --> 00:02:43.434
Your turn. Say: Confidence.

50
00:02:46.300 --> 00:02:47.301
Confidence.

51
00:02:48.050 --> 00:02:49.109
Self-aware.

52
00:02:50.117 --> 00:02:53.300
Self-aware means knowing your own feelings and character.

53
00:02:53.917 --> 00:02:56.543
Self-aware people know their strengths.

54
00:02:57.150 --> 00:02:59.976
Your turn. Say: Self-aware.

55
00:03:02.833 --> 00:03:03.927
Self-aware.

56
00:03:04.683 --> 00:03:05.510
Reflect.

57
00:03:06.517 --> 00:03:09.132
Reflect means to think carefully about something.

58
00:03:09.717 --> 00:03:11.937
I reflect on my day before I sleep.

59
00:03:12.550 --> 00:03:15.516
Your turn. Say: Reflect.

60
00:03:18.367 --> 00:03:19.298
Reflect.

61
00:03:20.050 --> 00:03:21.295
Growth mindset.

62
00:03:22.283 --> 00:03:25.165
Growth mindset means believing you can improve with effort.

63
00:03:25.750 --> 00:03:28.284
With a growth mindset, mistakes help you learn.

64
00:03:28.883 --> 00:03:31.907
Your turn. Say: Growth mindset.

65
00:03:34.767 --> 00:03:36.070
Growth mindset.

66
00:03:36.867 --> 00:03:40.587
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

67
00:03:41.450 --> 00:03:43.368
Visal, what makes you unique?

68
00:03:44.483 --> 00:03:48.886
I think my individuality comes from my values and my love of music.

69
00:03:49.983 --> 00:03:51.565
How do you express yourself?

70
00:03:52.650 --> 00:03:56.243
I express myself through songs. I write them myself!

71
00:03:57.350 --> 00:04:01.024
That's authentic self-expression. Are you self-aware?

72
00:04:02.117 --> 00:04:06.650
I try. I reflect every night, and I believe in myself more now.

73
00:04:07.800 --> 00:04:09.567
Part three: grammar.

74
00:04:10.417 --> 00:04:13.090
Grammar focus: Reflexive pronouns.

75
00:04:13.390 --> 00:04:14.623
Look at the pattern.

76
00:04:15.317 --> 00:04:16.701
I express myself.

77
00:04:17.617 --> 00:04:19.105
She believes in herself.

78
00:04:20.017 --> 00:04:22.167
We taught ourselves to play guitar.

79
00:04:23.133 --> 00:04:27.327
Use a reflexive pronoun when the subject and the object are the same person.

80
00:04:28.083 --> 00:04:31.455
Be careful! Don't say: She believes in her.

81
00:04:33.400 --> 00:04:35.899
Say: She believes in herself.

82
00:04:36.199 --> 00:04:39.313
Use a reflexive pronoun when it is the same person.

83
00:04:40.100 --> 00:04:43.008
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

84
00:04:43.800 --> 00:04:44.836
Who Am I?.

85
00:04:45.136 --> 00:04:48.366
My identity is shaped by my values and beliefs.

86
00:04:49.367 --> 00:04:53.061
Each person has unique personality traits and individuality.

87
00:04:54.067 --> 00:04:58.342
Being authentic and self-aware helps me express myself with confidence.

88
00:04:59.333 --> 00:05:02.122
I often reflect on what I have learned about myself.

89
00:05:03.133 --> 00:05:06.723
With a growth mindset, I believe in myself and keep growing.

90
00:05:07.833 --> 00:05:12.067
Part five: quiz. Three questions. Are you ready?

91
00:05:12.917 --> 00:05:14.487
She believes in blank.

92
00:05:14.787 --> 00:05:17.825
A, herself. B, her. C, himself.

93
00:05:21.367 --> 00:05:23.540
The answer is A: herself.

94
00:05:24.683 --> 00:05:26.636
Real and true to yourself is blank.

95
00:05:26.936 --> 00:05:31.089
A, authentic. B, unique. C, self-aware.

96
00:05:34.633 --> 00:05:36.633
The answer is A: authentic.

97
00:05:37.783 --> 00:05:40.294
Believing you can improve with effort is a blank.

98
00:05:40.594 --> 00:05:45.222
A, growth mindset. B, belief. C, identity.

99
00:05:48.767 --> 00:05:51.254
The answer is A: growth mindset.

100
00:05:52.467 --> 00:05:55.862
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

101
00:05:56.717 --> 00:05:58.612
What makes you unique as a person?

102
00:06:07.417 --> 00:06:08.859
Now listen to Visal.

103
00:06:09.159 --> 00:06:16.455
I think my kindness and my love of drawing make me unique. I express myself through art, and I am proud of myself.

104
00:06:16.755 --> 00:06:18.546
Excellent answer, Visal!

105
00:06:19.450 --> 00:06:24.204
Great work! Now you can use twelve new words and reflexive pronouns.

106
00:06:24.504 --> 00:06:28.793
Today's value is self-acceptance. Big or little, you are special.

107
00:06:29.093 --> 00:06:31.606
See you in Unit two. Goodbye!

108
00:06:31.906 --> 00:06:35.011
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

